1
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,280
♪Beneath the mask♪

2
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:12,480
♪Lies another mask♪
(Original Story: Haishi Lisheng)

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,320
♪Who's sincere♪

4
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:19,200
♪Who's only pretending♪

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,800
♪Borrowing your light♪

6
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:26,360
♪I walk through my own night♪

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,080
♪You are my weakness♪

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,720
♪And my weapon too♪

9
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,200
♪Draped in your shadow♪

10
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,200
♪I walk the blade's edge♪

11
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:34,880
♪If one day♪

12
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,640
♪The mask shatters♪

13
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,000
♪Will you still♪

14
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:42,480
♪Recognize my light♪

15
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,480
=The Masked Lover=

16
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,359
Careful! Easy now.

17
00:00:47,479 --> 00:00:49,840
These were all imported from the West.

18
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:50,600
Take it slow.

19
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:51,399
Butler Zhou.

20
00:00:52,079 --> 00:00:52,840
Lady Feng.

21
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:54,799
What's all this?

22
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,759
The governor sent Adjutant He

23
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:58,759
to buy clothes and jewelry for Ms. Lu.

24
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,799
They're all Western imports,

25
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:00,840
so handle them carefully.

26
00:01:04,359 --> 00:01:04,640
Come on.

27
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:05,439
Easy. Easy.

28
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:06,200
Keep up.

29
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:09,160
=Episode 5=

30
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:22,159
They're just clothes and jewelry.

31
00:01:22,239 --> 00:01:23,840
Why get so angry, Lady Feng?

32
00:01:25,439 --> 00:01:27,280
The governor is willing
to spend money on her

33
00:01:27,439 --> 00:01:29,400
because he believes she's his daughter.

34
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,400
(Que'er)
Once we find enough evidence...

35
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:35,439
Think about it, Lady Feng.

36
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:36,760
You know what the governor is like.

37
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,519
Would he tolerate being deceived?

38
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,159
He'd shoot her dead on the spot.

39
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,640
No matter how much Adjutant He
favors her, it won't help then.

40
00:01:55,159 --> 00:01:56,319
So,

41
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,000
clothes and jewelry don't matter.

42
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,319
What matters now

43
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:02,359
is getting Adjutant He to agree

44
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:04,040
to give you a child.

45
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,959
The Governor's Residence will someday
belong to the young master.

46
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:09,039
With his limited abilities,

47
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,879
he'll have to do whatever
Adjutant He says.

48
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:13,800
Once you have Adjutant He's child,

49
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,319
you'll have anything you want.

50
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:35,120
(Eight Years Earlier)
(Heaven and earth created mankind.)

51
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:37,759
(Young Su Yutang)
(Men and women are equal.)

52
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,680
(Young Lin Kefu)
(In the past, girls rarely studied.)

53
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:44,960
(They were confined to their homes.)

54
00:02:45,159 --> 00:02:46,000
(You two again?)

55
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,479
(Listening in without paying tuition?)

56
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,680
They say learning teaches
right from wrong.

57
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,599
Teaching others is a noble deed.

58
00:03:01,719 --> 00:03:03,840
So why should we have to pay to learn?

59
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:08,400
Because teachers
need food and clothes too.

60
00:03:09,479 --> 00:03:10,240
Fine.

61
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,319
Once we've learned every magic trick,

62
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,639
we can perform with the troupe.

63
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:15,479
Then we'll earn enough for tuition.

64
00:03:16,439 --> 00:03:17,560
By then,

65
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,280
we'll already be grown up.

66
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:21,599
Look at the children in that school.

67
00:03:21,759 --> 00:03:23,199
They're about our age.

68
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,400
We're still bound to fall behind them.

69
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:29,759
I wish school were free.

70
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:33,240
I wish the rich would show some kindness

71
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,879
and let every child go to school.

72
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,479
Now that's a fine piece.

73
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,680
Here.

74
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,520
Sir.

75
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,199
What did that young woman pawn?

76
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,519
Are you looking to buy it?

77
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,319
Thank you.

78
00:04:28,839 --> 00:04:30,600
Could you take a look

79
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,160
and tell me what these are worth?

80
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,880
(2,000 taels)

81
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,360
Ms. Lu, you mean you'll pay for

82
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:50,319
the children in the troupe
to go to school?

83
00:04:51,279 --> 00:04:52,079
Yes.

84
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,160
But don't worry, Troupe Master.

85
00:04:54,279 --> 00:04:56,519
I just want them to learn to read

86
00:04:56,519 --> 00:04:58,040
and understand right from wrong.

87
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,639
It won't take much of their time.

88
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,000
They can still

89
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,639
keep training as usual

90
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,360
and doing their usual chores.

91
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,240
Your kindness, Ms. Lu,

92
00:05:07,759 --> 00:05:09,160
is a blessing for these children.

93
00:05:10,759 --> 00:05:11,560
Of course,

94
00:05:11,959 --> 00:05:14,480
if any child shows
real academic promise,

95
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,120
don't hold them back.

96
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,680
I'll cover all their expenses.

97
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,480
Please see to it.

98
00:05:21,839 --> 00:05:22,920
Of course.

99
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,000
Naturally.

100
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:27,600
(The Stage Bears a Nation's Spirit)

101
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,319
By the way,

102
00:05:28,319 --> 00:05:30,040
I remember years ago,

103
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,920
there was a girl here named Rong.

104
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,079
Then she disappeared.

105
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:36,560
Do you know how she's doing now?

106
00:05:37,519 --> 00:05:38,600
Who cares?

107
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:41,199
That no-good girl
was lazy and shiftless,

108
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,639
and she stole things too.

109
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,600
So...

110
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:48,160
you never saw her again?

111
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,120
No.

112
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:51,839
Someone like her?

113
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:54,199
Our troupe wanted
nothing to do with her.

114
00:05:55,959 --> 00:05:58,399
Why ask about her all of a sudden?

115
00:05:59,879 --> 00:06:00,639
Nothing.

116
00:06:00,959 --> 00:06:03,079
She just crossed my mind,
so I thought I'd ask.

117
00:06:03,639 --> 00:06:04,560
You see,

118
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,079
someone like her

119
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,160
(The Stage Bears a Nation's Spirit)
might've turned out differently

120
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:09,000
if she'd had more schooling.

121
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,040
Maybe she wouldn't have turned to theft.

122
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,920
The way I see it,

123
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,040
people really are born different.

124
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,120
Some people are just base by nature.

125
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,560
You never went to school either, Ms. Lu,

126
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,279
but...

127
00:06:22,279 --> 00:06:24,240
you're just a pearl dulled by dust.

128
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:26,959
You have a heart that cares for others

129
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,399
and a noble character.

130
00:06:33,439 --> 00:06:34,240
No.

131
00:06:36,199 --> 00:06:37,680
Everyone is born equal.

132
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,680
(Lu)

133
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:01,800
There's something I don't understand.

134
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,279
Why do you always practice shooting
at night?

135
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,000
Isn't it too dark?

136
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,800
I'm more likely to shoot at night.

137
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:11,959
That makes sense.

138
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,319
But you're improving quickly.

139
00:07:14,519 --> 00:07:15,680
You don't have to push so hard.

140
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,600
I want every shot to hit its mark.

141
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,199
That's quite an ambition.

142
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,480
But that takes time.

143
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,199
You can't rush it.

144
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,480
I don't have much time left.

145
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,560
The old man's birthday is next month.

146
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,120
I want this to be his birthday gift.

147
00:07:36,439 --> 00:07:38,319
If you hadn't told me,
I'd have thought...

148
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,480
Thought what?

149
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:44,000
That you were training so hard

150
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:46,480
because you hoped that one day,

151
00:07:47,079 --> 00:07:49,399
even if the old man found out
you're not his biological daughter,

152
00:07:49,879 --> 00:07:51,000
he still couldn't bring himself
to kill you.

153
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:57,160
Only you have leverage over me,
Adjutant He.

154
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,959
As long as you keep quiet,

155
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:00,480
how would the old man ever know?

156
00:08:02,839 --> 00:08:03,639
Come here.

157
00:08:06,439 --> 00:08:08,199
You've got the basics Zhaolin taught you

158
00:08:08,399 --> 00:08:10,000
down solid.

159
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,120
You're just missing one trick.

160
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,120
Want to know it?

161
00:08:15,519 --> 00:08:16,279
Yes.

162
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,600
(Governor's Residence)
Come in, everyone.

163
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,759
Right this way.

164
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,199
Staff Officer Chen. It's been a while.

165
00:08:25,199 --> 00:08:26,560
Butler Zhou. It's been a while.

166
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:28,600
Please, come inside.

167
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,079
(Gentle Breezes Bring Harmony)

168
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:32,240
When the time comes,

169
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:34,039
wait by the western steps.

170
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:35,200
When she falls,

171
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,120
move in and cover for her immediately.

172
00:08:36,399 --> 00:08:37,480
Take her straight to the hospital.

173
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,519
Don't let anyone see through the act.

174
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:40,759
Be careful.

175
00:08:41,279 --> 00:08:42,080
Yes.

176
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,639
Lady Feng.

177
00:08:48,639 --> 00:08:49,399
It's getting late.

178
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:51,120
The governor is waiting
for your birthday wishes.

179
00:09:01,159 --> 00:09:02,080
You may go.

180
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,759
Take the western steps later.

181
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,399
Pretend to take a fall.

182
00:09:28,399 --> 00:09:29,159
No.

183
00:09:32,559 --> 00:09:34,120
Now that I'm pregnant,

184
00:09:34,159 --> 00:09:35,360
he won't touch me,

185
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:36,679
and he gives me whatever I want.

186
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,679
I don't want to give that up.

187
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,080
Don't worry.

188
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,440
My men will cover for you.

189
00:09:44,159 --> 00:09:45,440
I've arranged your escape.

190
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:46,600
If you stay

191
00:09:46,799 --> 00:09:48,600
until he realizes

192
00:09:48,759 --> 00:09:50,159
there's no baby,

193
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,440
no one will be able to save you.

194
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:09,720
Lady Feng, you can't lose the baby.

195
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:10,759
If you do,

196
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:13,120
the governor
will blame your carelessness.

197
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,320
More importantly,

198
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,399
you'll no longer have a reason

199
00:10:15,399 --> 00:10:16,840
to ask Adjutant He for a child.

200
00:10:19,559 --> 00:10:21,000
Adjutant He cares about you.

201
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,799
He couldn't bear to see
anything happen to you.

202
00:10:23,159 --> 00:10:24,639
Give him a few days to come around,

203
00:10:24,799 --> 00:10:27,000
and he'll agree to give you a child.

204
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:37,600
(Longevity)

205
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,799
I have twelve bullets.

206
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,919
Each point stands for one year.

207
00:10:42,919 --> 00:10:43,960
My total score

208
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,080
will show how devoted
I am to you, Father.

209
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:49,039
This is my birthday gift to you.

210
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,120
Good.

211
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,240
(All your life,)

212
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,519
(have you ever hated anyone?)

213
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:04,519
(Imagine that spot is his heart.)

214
00:11:04,679 --> 00:11:08,240
(Then imagine there's only one bullet
in your gun.)

215
00:11:08,639 --> 00:11:10,559
(Heaven has given you only one chance.)

216
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:17,200
♪Blades clash, leaving us both trapped♪

217
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:20,360
♪Nightmares from days gone by♪

218
00:11:23,039 --> 00:11:24,159
(So there really is someone.)

219
00:11:25,159 --> 00:11:27,200
(Who do you hate so bitterly?)

220
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,520
♪Unveiling all the absurdity♪

221
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,760
♪Seeking love's only truth♪

222
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:40,440
♪Through fate's layered maze♪

223
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:44,040
♪Charging toward the unknown♪

224
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,240
(I did it.)

225
00:11:48,799 --> 00:11:49,639
Reporting, Governor.

226
00:11:49,639 --> 00:11:51,279
A total of 100 points.

227
00:11:52,519 --> 00:11:54,600
May you live to a hundred, Father.

228
00:11:55,159 --> 00:11:58,600
Long life to the Governor!

229
00:11:58,919 --> 00:12:01,440
Long life to the Governor!

230
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,120
Father.

231
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:06,639
When did you secretly get so good
at shooting?

232
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:07,960
Guess.

233
00:12:09,399 --> 00:12:11,159
You've really got a good eye.

234
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,519
She's got some real skill.

235
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,960
Ms. Lu's gift was certainly unique.

236
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,519
We can't be outdone.

237
00:12:19,759 --> 00:12:22,679
I spent six months learning
to paint this.

238
00:12:22,799 --> 00:12:25,320
I made it especially for your birthday.

239
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,120
I had no idea

240
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,080
Lady Feng had secretly learned to paint.

241
00:12:29,559 --> 00:12:31,120
Two monkeys.

242
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,360
The Buddha.

243
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,440
This is...

244
00:12:33,759 --> 00:12:37,799
The Six-Eared Macaque
fighting Sun Wukong.

245
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:41,919
The Six-Eared Macaque tried
to pass himself off as the real one,

246
00:12:42,159 --> 00:12:44,679
only to die beneath the Buddha's palm.

247
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,039
Governor, you're devoted to your people.

248
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,480
And you're valiant and decisive,

249
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:51,320
just like the Buddha in this painting.

250
00:12:51,879 --> 00:12:54,399
Well said. The painting's even better.

251
00:12:54,519 --> 00:12:55,960
Yanyan, you've put a lot into this.

252
00:12:57,159 --> 00:12:58,039
Governor.

253
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,440
There are so many people here today.

254
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:00,759
Given my condition,

255
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:01,960
I'll excuse myself.

256
00:13:02,039 --> 00:13:03,000
Go get some rest.

257
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:02,080
♪A lie carved deep into the heart♪
(Loyalty Eternal)

258
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:06,720
♪Blades clash, leaving us both trapped♪

259
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,880
♪Nightmares from days gone by♪

260
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,400
♪Love and hate intertwine♪

261
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:16,760
♪In eyes ignited by sparks♪

262
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:22,720
♪Each blooming with a fierce edge♪

263
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:27,440
♪Shattering moonlight on the ground♪

264
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:30,920
♪I look up and meet your gaze♪

265
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,240
♪Unveiling all the absurdity♪

266
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:36,480
♪Seeking love's only truth♪

267
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:43,160
♪Through fate's layered maze♪

268
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,760
♪Charging toward the unknown♪

269
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:49,960
♪Don't forget your stubborn heart♪

270
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:56,480
♪Fire tempers the strength to go on♪

271
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,880
♪Counting down the long night's haze♪

272
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:03,200
♪With my own hands, I draw the dawn♪

273
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:06,040
♪Boundless♪
